WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:04.771 align:start size:78% position:22% line:0%
- Hello, I'm Gav.
- I'm Dan.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.572 size:88% position:44% line:0%
Welcome to "Planet Slow Mo."

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:09.609 align:start position:0% line:0%
You may have noticed
that A, we're dressed
like firefighters.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- All right.
  Oh, that's pretty hot!
- Let's head outside.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.636
Gav:
This is our experiment area.

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start position:0%
Dan, why don't you run us
through this shipping
container setup?

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.176 align:start size:72% position:28% line:0%
Okay, so the fire
is gonna be all inside.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.777 align:start size:75% position:25%
Important things to know
on the outside, though,

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:47.346 align:start size:97% position:3%
are these doors here,
which can be closed and opened.

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:69% position:31%
Moving along,
also there's a window,

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.584 align:start size:63% position:38%
one on each side,
that can be closed
and opened as well.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:78% position:22%
And we've got this
Dutch door-- Dutch oven--

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:84% position:16%
- What is it? Dutch--
- Not Dutch oven.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:57.857 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Just Dutch door.
- Just the door, yeah.

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.225 align:start size:66% position:34%
Dutch door situation.

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:00.693 align:start size:56% position:44%
I'll get into that
in a minute.

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:02.228 align:start size:50% position:50%
Let's go inside.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:07.700 align:start size:59% position:41%
Inside you'll see
our extremely nice,

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:47% position:53%
but extremely
flammable room.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:72% position:28%
Wood all over the walls
as fuel.

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:12.839 align:start size:66% position:34%
Very flammable couch.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.209 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
Dead Christmas tree.
They go up like an absolute.

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:19.212 align:start size:66% position:34% line:0%
A backdraft is caused
when there's a fire
in a contained area.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.681 align:start size:69% position:31%
Eventually the fire
will deplete all
the oxygen in the room

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:25.718 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it dies down,
but it's still sort of
burning the fuel as embers.

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:28.187 align:start size:75% position:25%
And then what can happen
is a window might break

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:75% position:25%
or a door flies open,
causing a sudden rush
of oxygen into the room,

00:01:31.757 --> 00:01:35.228 align:start size:75% position:25%
which then causes
a very deadly explosion.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:38.431 align:start size:69% position:31%
Firefighters typically
do everything they can
to avoid a backdraft

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:41.267 align:start size:78% position:22%
and we're here today
deliberately causing one.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start position:0%
Yeah, the way
we're gonna manage that is

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:44.403 align:start position:0%
we've mentioned this
fuel at the back,

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:45.404 align:start position:0%
the Christmas tree
and the wood.

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:46.539 align:start position:0%
We're gonna light that.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:47.874 align:start position:0%
And when
that's nicely cooking,

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.809 align:start position:0%
we're gonna shut
the back doors up,

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.878 align:start position:0%
and then the fire
is gonna start to move
through the--

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.579 align:start position:0%
through the room,
onto the sofa,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:55.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
- onto the couch, you know.
- Ahh.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.884 align:start position:0%
All that,
and it's gonna move through,

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start position:0%
and then we'll have
some flames coming out
the windows just here.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.587 align:start position:0%
Gonna move further
through the room.

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.489
We're gonna close
the windows up,

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.825 align:start position:0%
and then the only thing
that's gonna be open
is this front door.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:09.762 align:start size:78% position:22%
So we've got our fire.
It's nice and hot,
about a thousand degrees.

00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:11.397 size:84% position:58%
It's come through the room,

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.332 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all that's gonna be open
is this bottom door here,

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.501 align:start size:72% position:28%
allowing the oxygen in,
getting the fire nice

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.503 align:start size:53% position:47%
and thoroughly
cooking the room.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:18.938 size:84% position:58%
Then we're gonna close this

00:02:18.971 --> 00:02:20.873 align:start size:66% position:34%
and start to
deplete it of oxygen.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.276 align:start size:47% position:53%
At that point,
we'll then open
this top door,

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.877 align:start size:56% position:44%
and then within
sort of 30 seconds

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:69% position:31%
of smoke pouring out
and oxygen pouring in,

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.248 align:start size:75% position:25%
it's gonna create
our backdraft explosion.

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.617 align:start position:0%
To measure how far
the backdraft goes,

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.419 align:start position:0%
